   "line": 10092,
   "text": "Thus $H_2'-de+ad+ae$ is still nonplanar, and both tests in\n\\eqref{r1:c1-caps} still fail for $B'$.\nIn the nonplanar case, $H_2'$ lies in their common subgraph,\nso again both tests fail.\n\nThe reduction keeps all four attachments and a connected interior\nwith at most nine vertices. Therefore\n$G'=(\\Psi_3\\cup B')+bd+E$ is a nontoroidal minor with at most\n$18$ vertices, and minimality gives $G'=G$.\nConstruction~\\ref{common:marked-construction}, using $E'$ and\nrequiring $de$ when $H_0$ is planar, therefore includes every\npossibility. The two choices of $E$ and the two subdivision\ncases give $66{,}384$ candidates.\nEvery resulting graph is toroidal, has a $K_5$ minor or a proper\nnontoroidal minor, or is one of thirteen graphs $\\mathfrak T_i$~\\supp{E30}."
  }
 ],
